1
00:00:00,103 --> 00:00:05,368
Learning with a Purpose Initially many students regard a diploma as their

2
00:00:05,382 --> 00:00:11,026
ultimate objective Yet a qualification is only one component of an education

3
00:00:11,934 --> 00:00:16,579
What matters more is whether learners can interpret a difficult paragraph formulate

4
00:00:16,592 --> 00:00:21,592
a coherent argument and apply an abstract concept to a realistic situation

5
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:26,290
A good instructor will therefore encourage a student to question an assumption

6
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:31,118
clarify a notion and distinguish an apparent fact from a reasonable inference

7
00:00:32,026 --> 00:00:37,684
At our college each participant must undertake a small research project Students

8
00:00:37,697 --> 00:00:42,618
first prepare an outline then develop a hypothesis and gather empirical evidence

9
00:00:43,526 --> 00:00:46,987
They submit a draft to a tutor who may reject a superficial

10
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:53,342
explanation but will offer constructive counsel A scholarship rewards persistence and integrity

11
00:00:53,355 --> 00:00:57,816
as well as achievement The dean hopes that this systematic approach will

12
00:00:57,829 --> 00:01:04,342
broaden students' intellectual interests Not only does purposeful study deepen understanding but

13
00:01:04,355 --> 00:01:09,855
it also gives learners the confidence to tackle unfamiliar problems A university

14
00:01:09,868 --> 00:01:14,408
should cultivate independent judgment rather than make perfection its only criterion of

15
00:01:14,421 --> 00:01:15,237
success

